          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Given a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} class
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            will already have some colimits, which we wish to preserve. A
            %strong conservative cocompletion
            of a category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            is a cocompletion that preserves the colimits in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %p
            For a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            with
            = succeed "-colimits," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              \-conservative cocompletion
            (for a class
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            of colimits). It is the the full subcategory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mo ∘
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Set
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^\circ, Set]_\Phi
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            spanned by the functors sending
            = succeed "-colimits" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            to limits in the presheaf category.
          %p
            For a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large category
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+presheaves"} small presheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+categories"} locally small categories
            that do not admit locally small conservative cocompletions (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AV02"} AV02
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            is a class of colimiting cocones in a category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            = succeed "-colimit-preserving" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                  %mo :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j:C\to D
            exhibits a cocomplete category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            as a
            %strong
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
              \-conservative cocompletion
            if, for any cocomplete category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
            induces an equivalence between the category of
            = succeed "-colimit-preserving" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to E
            and the category of small-colimit-preserving functors
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D\to E
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
          %p
            Then the
            %strong conservative cocompletion
            (with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            unspecified) is the
            = succeed "-conservative" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Φ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Φ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            the class of all colimiting cocones in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h2#properties Properties
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For a small category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cont
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cont(C^op, Set)
                is
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete"} complete
                and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete"} cocomplete
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi Cont
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \to Cont(C^op, Set)
                creates limits and colimits. Consequently, every small category may be continuously and cocontinuously fully embedded into a complete and cocomplete locally small category. (Note that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Cont
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cont(C^op, Set)
                will rarely be
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+category"} closed
                unless
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is (
                %a{:href => "https://mathoverflow.net/a/185024"}> counterexample
                ).) However, not every locally small category admits such an embedding: see Example III.1 of
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "#T66"} Trnková 1966
            %li
              %p
                For a small category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "-conservative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective subcategory
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [C^op,Set]
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+subcategory+problem"} orthogonal subcategory problem
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Cont
                        %mi Φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cont_\Phi(C^op,Set)
                comprises those presheaves that are orthogonal to the canonical natural transformation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi colim
                        %mi i
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim_i C(-,a_i)\to C(-,\colim_i a_i)
                for every diagram
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_i)
                in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is small and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c\otimes -)
                preserves
                = succeed "-colimits," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} monoidal closed
                structure on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Cont
                        %mi Φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cont_\Phi(C^op, Set)
                such that the Yoneda embedding
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi Cont
                        %mi Φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to Cont_\Phi(C^op, Set)
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+monoidal+functor"} strong monoidal
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is already
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+closed+category"} cartesian closed
                or symmetric monoidal closed, so too is
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Cont
                          %mi Φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cont_\Phi(C^op, Set)
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi c
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (c\otimes -)
                is a left adjoint then it necessarily
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoints+preserve+%28co-%29limits"}
                    preserves
                    %em all
                    colimits
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Day+convolution"} Day convolution
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi Cont
                          %mi Φ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Set
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cont_\Phi(C^op, Set)
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ψ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
                be a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sound+doctrine+of+limits"} sound doctrine of limits
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is small and has all
                = succeed "-colimits," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Ψ
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi^{op}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                be the class of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ψ
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi^{op}
                colimiting cocones in
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                = succeed "-conservative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is also the free
                = succeed "-filtered" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Ψ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                (see Theorem 5.5 of
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#ABLR02"} ABLR02
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                The category of finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattices"} semilattices
                is the conservative cocompletion of the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relations"} relations
                under finite colimits (and also its
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
                under
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflexive+coequalisers"} reflexive coequalisers
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#AMMU14"} AMMU14
            %li
              %p
                The category
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pos"} Pos
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partial+orders"} partial orders
                is the free conservative cocompletion of the category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+orders"} total orders
                (
                %a{:href => "#Tataru24"}> Tataru24
                ).
            %li
              %p
                A small category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                with a class of limit cones
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                is also called a ‘realized limit
                = succeed "\u2019." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sketch"} sketch
                = succeed "-conservative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Φ
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi^op
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mi op
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^op
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finitely+presentable+category"} locally finitely presentable category
                is the
                = succeed "-conservative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                is the class of finite colimit cones. More generally a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+category"}
                  locally
                  = succeed "-presentable" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi κ
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                is the
                = succeed "-conservative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                = succeed "-compact" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                is the class of
                = succeed "-small" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                be a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lawvere+theory"} Lawvere theory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                be the class of finite
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coproducts"} coproducts
                cones in
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{op}
                (equivalently, finite copowers). Then the
                = succeed "-conservative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi L
                        %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^{op}
                is the category of
                = succeed "-algebras." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
                = succeed "-conservative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinStoch"} FinStoch
                is the category of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+space"} abstract convex sets
                = succeed "-conservative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinRel"} FinRel
                is the category of join
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattices"} semilattices
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebraic+theories"} commutative algebraic theories
                = succeed "-algebras." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi L
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %li
              %p
                Since categories of algebras are typically not cartesian closed, the previous point illustrates that
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi Cont
                        %mi Φ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Set
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cont_\Phi(C^op,Set)
                is not cartesian closed in general (e.g.
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoids"} monoids
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groups"} groups
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+sets"} convex sets
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rings"} rings
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                be a small
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+category"} extensive category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Φ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                be the class of finite coproduct cones. The category of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves"} sheaves
                for the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extensive+coverage"} extensive coverage
                is the
                = succeed "-conservative" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Φ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Phi
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi C
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Joachim+Lambek"}> Joachim Lambek
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Completions of categories: Seminar lectures given 1966 in Zürich
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0077265"} doi
            %li#T66
              %p
                Věra Trnková,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Limits in categories and limit-preserving functors
            %li
              %p
                J. F Kennison,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em On limit-preserving functors
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Max+Kelly"}> Max Kelly
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Basic Concepts of Enriched Category Theory
                = succeed "." do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.tac.mta.ca/tac/reprints/articles/10/tr10.pdf"} TAC reprint
            %li#AV02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C4%B1%CC%81+Ad%C3%A1mek"} Jiřı́ Adámek
                and
                = succeed "." do
                  %span.newWikiWord
                    Jiřı́ Velebil
                    %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Ji%C5%99%C4%B1%CC%81+Velebil"} ?
                = succeed "." do
                  %em A remark on conservative cocompletions of categories
          %p See also Theorem 11.5 of the following notes, where cartesian closedness is discussed.
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marcelo+Fiore"}> Marcelo Fiore
              \.
              = succeed "." do
                %em Enrichment and representation theorems for categories of domains and continuous functions
              %a{:href => "http://www.cl.cam.ac.uk/~mpf23/papers/ADT/rep.ps.gz"} PS.GZ file
          %p The symmetric monoidal case is discussed and proved in Lemma 4.6 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mathys+Rennela"} Mathys Rennela
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sam+Staton"} Sam Staton
              = succeed "." do
                %em Classical Control, Quantum Circuits and Linear Logic in Enriched Category Theory
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.05159"} arxiv:1711.05159
          %p See section 6.4 (and Theorem 6.4.3 in particular) of:
          %ul
            %li#MakkaiPare
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Makkai"}> Michael Makkai
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+Par%C3%A9"} Robert Paré
              = succeed "," do
                %em Accessible categories: The foundations of categorical model theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/conm-104"} ISBN:978-0-8218-7692-3
          %p For examples:
          %ul
            %li#AMMU14
              %p Adámek, J., Myers, R. S., Urbat, H., &amp; Milius, S. “On continuous nondeterminism and state minimality.” Electronic Notes in Theoretical Computer Science 308 (2014): 3-23.
            %li
              %p Mimram, Samuel, and Cinzia Di Giusto. “A categorical theory of patches.” Electronic notes in theoretical computer science 298 (2013): 283-307.
            %li#Tataru24
              %p
                Calin Tataru, “Partial orders are the free conservative cocompletion of total orders.”
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.12924"} arXiv:2404.12924
                (2024).
          %p Sound doctrines of limits:
          %ul
            %li#ABLR02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ji%C5%99%C3%AD+Ad%C3%A1mek"}> Jiří Adámek
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"} Francis Borceux
              = succeed "," do
